stt: user preference + pinning (deferred, low urgency)

/transcribe is the one surface that still resolves its own default at call time
(`registry.registry.default(SURFACE_STT)` in retrieval/service.py). Every other
surface either carries a pin from the gateway (chat/generate/editor), from the
job payload (ingest, vision), or from the workspace (embedding).

Why it is not a billing hole today: CreditsForTranscribe prices per second of
audio, not per token, and it does not read the model at all. So a default that
moves mid-request changes which model runs but not what the user is charged, and
the charge stays correct either way. That stops being true the moment STT rates
become per-model — the price and the pin have to land in the same change.

To do, when STT becomes user-selectable:

1. users.stt_model_key (+ default, + check), like editor_model_key.
2. Gateway resolves it and hands the pin to /transcribe, the way chat does.
3. resolve_pinned on the pipeline side (it is already strict; just stop calling
   .default()).
4. Price per model in CreditsForTranscribe, keeping duration as the unit.
5. Settings → LLM picker + ModelPicker surface, messages/{en,zh}.json.
6. Ops dashboard: STT joins the user-facing keys that a deprecation must remap
   (see todo-ops-dashboard §6.3).
